      "artist": "Infrogmation",
      "description": "New Orleans after Hurricane Katrina: Sign at an entrance to Jackson Barracks, a military base in New Orleans established after the War of 1812. National Guard troops and relief supplies were stationed here for Hurricane Katrina. As this section of the city, in the Lower 9th Ward, was one of the first to flood catastrophically, troops had their hands full saving themselves in the disaster. Some succeeded in launching boats and helping save people in the neighborhood, but much equipment and supplies were lost.\nNote lines  of various levels of long standing water can be seen. Highest water was a rapidly rising storm surge which necessitated people effect to either run upstairs in multi story buildings where that was an option or swim for their lives.",
